{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1406137-taking-lilith-as-a-totem-patron","id":1406137,"title":"Taking Lilith as a Totem/Patron?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-03T13:00:16-07:00","id":1406137,"title":"Taking Lilith as a Totem/Patron?","content":"I have been doing some heavy research for the Order of Hermes for an upcoming Chronicle I am writing, by watching Youtube videos while working, with a heavy emphasis on Goetia. I've learned that Demons are apparently super helpful and friendly when summoned, Lucifer is everyone's friend and mentor, and Lilith makes for a great drinking buddy and match maker. Seriously, though, apparently Lilith is super important to people who think they are Astral Projecting, and I am now interested in including her as a prominent figure of reverence in my upcoming story. Can there be an archetypal spirit Lilith on top of the Oracle or whatever the Vampire Lilith is? I want to make a &quot;realistic&quot; presentation of Goetia, and demons, djinn, Lucifer, and Lilith all figure prominently as mentors and spirit guides to people studying Goetia. Any thoughts on how I can present Lilith as someone worthy of having her own shrine in the Chantry and being summoned/channeled by a Cabal dedicated to Goetia? I want her to be a shadowy patron and guide for the Cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-03-2020, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T13:35:08-07:00","id":1406142,"title":"","content":"Short answer is yes that Lilith could be a patron and guide for characters.<br /> <br /> There are many takes on her. Maybe check out Infernalism: The Book of Screams for some ideas. Page 129 of M20 Book of the Fallen has about a paragraph on Lillianism.<br /> <br /> Outside of Mage, Lilith is a superior for the concept of Freedom in the In Nomine game where you play angels or demons. You can find her book on Warehouse 23 (Steve Jackson Games did the English translations of In Nomine) or on Drivethrurpg.com<br /> <br /> Ken Hite also had a couple versions of Lilith in one of his 'Ken Writes About Stuff' for Pelgrane Press. That's a single volume 'Lilith' or part of a larger volume.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T15:45:07-07:00","id":1406161,"title":"","content":"If it is a Hermetic Chantry, then such a shrine would likely have <i>House Quaesitor</i> asking lots of questions - in a very pointed manor - about a breach of the second clause of the <i>The Code of Hermes</i>; on grounds of Infernalism. So would likely have to keep all of it very quiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:09:54-07:00","id":1406164,"title":"","content":"Is Lilith really an infernal being? It seems like ALL Hermetics want to be like Lilith, minus the enlightenment through agony thing. They want to be above Heaven and Hell, and command both the divine and infernal. That is Lilith to a tee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:24:37-07:00","id":1406169,"title":"","content":"NA..........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:34:25-07:00","id":1406176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1406137-taking-lilith-as-a-totem-patron?p=1406164#post1406164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Lilith really an infernal being? It seems like ALL Hermetics want to be like Lilith, minus the enlightenment through agony thing. They want to be above Heaven and Hell, and command both the divine and infernal. That is Lilith to a tee.</div> </div> </div> </div>All hermetics want to be like Hermes, the sage. Yes Lilith is an infernal being at worst, read M20 book of the fallen. At best shes a proto verbena, and well if you want to worship her there is a tradition for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 08-03-2020, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:50:31-07:00","id":1406178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1406137-taking-lilith-as-a-totem-patron?p=1406176#post1406176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All hermetics want to be like Hermes, the sage. Yes Lilith is an infernal being at worst, read M20 book of the fallen. At best shes a proto verbena, and well if you want to worship her there is a tradition for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is less about worshiping her and more about wanting to keep Goetia close to its source material. In the modern world, Lilith is looked up to as a guide for your Goetian on the go. She is supposedly someone you can contact on the Astral Plane, who will dispense advice and magical instruction for those who impress her. Obviously, I can't have Lucifer and the lords of Hell show up the way Goetians seem to imagine them, as helpful guides, because WoD deals in a hard black and white in regards to the Infernal, but Lilith seems like she might be the one gray area in all of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:55:44-07:00","id":1406182,"title":"","content":"She was kicked out of eden and cursed by god to forever wander the earth unloved. Also modern goeta mixes a lot of new age feminist type magic in it. Go old goeta, better yet look at the section on it in the back of Blood Treachery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T17:42:37-07:00","id":1406191,"title":"","content":"There are times when designing your chronicle that the ST must make a decision about certain key elements of their setting because it does have a relevant impact on the PCs. This sounds like one of them.<br /> <br /> I personally wouldn't make Lilith as an acceptable guide in any of my chronicles. She seems distinctly infernal. She was certainly seen as malevolent by the ancient peoples - she kills babies, hangs out with demons, steals life from men, and corrupts people. All the modern occult and feminist interpretation are just misguided interpretations that covers up her actual role. Those people who think she's helpful are fools. They are playing with fire, but don't know it.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't need to be the role in <i>your</i> own chronicle. If you want a more ambivalent or beneficial interpretation, you can do that. However, I would create some kind of explanation for objections PCs and NPCs might have. So maybe all these negative stories aren't true (though some of them could be). Or there is some other spirit that is negative which gets conflated with Lilith, but the &quot;real&quot; Lilith isn't that. She might just be a &quot;neutral' or ambivalent spirit that can be used by either side, thus explaining bad things while allowing you to use her in another way.<br /> <br /> You determine what the ultimate truths of the world in your chronicles. You just have to watch out for any major player objections if you do something that greatly contradicts how they think it should be handled because they'll lead to OOC problems. You know your players better than any of us on the boards, so you should know whether this presents and problem, or if your PCs will just go with that interpretation or at least be open to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T18:15:14-07:00","id":1406197,"title":"","content":"In Nominee's take on Lilith doesn't make her nice. However, she's for Freedom and that makes her more likely for RPG gamers to want to play her than some of the other demons. And some of the angels in In Nominee are pretty nasty.<br /> <br /> With any religious material, it's good to know who is writing it and why and the level of the writer's erudition and research effort before incorporating it into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T07:06:33-07:00","id":1406263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1406137-taking-lilith-as-a-totem-patron#post1406137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can there be an archetypal spirit Lilith on top of the Oracle or whatever the Vampire Lilith is? (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Any reasons why you can't have them worship / pay homage to Lilith the Mage <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/1/18/Lilith_garden.png/revision/latest?cb=20140501181052\" target=\"_blank\">https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/...20140501181052</a> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-04-2020, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T11:38:49-07:00","id":1406306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1406137-taking-lilith-as-a-totem-patron?p=1406263#post1406263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reasons why you can't have them worship / pay homage to Lilith the Mage <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/1/18/Lilith_garden.png/revision/latest?cb=20140501181052\" target=\"_blank\">https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/...20140501181052</a> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hermetics don\u2019t worship. Honor and respect as a mentor is probably as far as they would be willing to go. And I want a spirit rather than a physical being. It seems to be more in line with Goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T13:53:21-07:00","id":1406326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1406137-taking-lilith-as-a-totem-patron?p=1406306#post1406306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hermetics don\u2019t worship. Honor and respect as a mentor is probably as far as they would be willing to go. And I want a spirit rather than a physical being. It seems to be more in line with Goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totem implies worship, now if they want a spirit of lilith just hanging around take it as an ally or mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}